{#
  view/j-user/users/edit.phtml — one account's form, plus the delete modal.

  **The `<h1>` is translated here and was not in the .phtml.** `escapeHtml($title)` with
  no `translate()`, next to a `headTitle($title)` the layout *does* translate — so a
  Spanish administrator got "Editar usuario" in the browser tab and "Edit User" on the
  page. The port that first moved this page to Twig reproduced that deliberately, because
  its only evidence that nothing else had moved was a byte-for-byte diff against the laminas
  rendering; the .phtml is gone now, so there is nothing left to be faithful to and the
  heading translates (2026-08-21).

  Measured across all five locales after the change: nine of the twelve non-English
  headings now differ from English. The one that does not is this page in Italian —
  "Edit User" is a separate phrase from "Edit user" and carries de/es/pt but no it_IT — so
  asking for the translation is what puts that one on the worklist rather than what fills
  it. (A note here claimed "Edit User" was untranslated in *all five*; that was wrong,
  taken from a backlog entry rather than from the rendering.)

  **No `action` attribute on the outer form**, hence `form_open(form, '')`: the .phtml never
  calls `setAttribute('action', …)`, so laminas emits none and the browser posts to the
  current URL. The modal's form is the opposite — it posts to a different route and carries
  one.

  `false` on the two selects is `$this->formSelect()->setTranslatorEnabled(false)`. Role
  names and person names are **data**, and translating data files one phrase row per row of
  the table. Labels are still translated; only the options are not.

  The delete button sits *inside* the outer form and opens the modal, so the modal's form is
  a sibling of it rather than a child: nesting forms is not legal HTML, which is why the
  modal markup comes after `form_close()`.
#}
{% extends juser_layout %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate(page_title) }}</h1>

{{ form_open(form, '') }}
{{ form_row(form.get('userId')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('username')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('email')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('displayName')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('rolesList'), false) }}
{% if show_person %}{{ form_row(form.get('personId'), false) }}{% endif %}
{{ form_row(form.get('isMultiPersonUser')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('emailVerified')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('active')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('security')) }}
{#- `?>` in the .phtml eats the newline that follows it, so laminas emits
    `</button>&nbsp;\n<button` and not `</button>\n&nbsp;\n<button`. One whitespace run
    fewer, and `&nbsp;` decodes to U+00A0 which the baseline harness deliberately does not
    collapse — so the difference is real bytes rather than formatting. Same below, twice. -#}
{{ form_submit(form.get('submit')) }}&nbsp;
<button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" data-toggle="modal" data-target="#deleteModal">{{ translate('Delete') }}</button>
{{ form_close() }}

<!-- Modal -->
<div class="modal fade bs-example-modal-sm" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" id="deleteModal"
aria-labelledby="mySmallModalLabel">
<div class="modal-dialog modal-sm">
<div class="modal-content">
<div class="modal-header">
<button type="button" class="close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"><span aria-hidden="true">&times;
</span></button>
<h4 class="modal-title">{{ translate('Careful') }}...</h4>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <p>{{ translate('You are about to delete %s')|format(user.username) }}</p>
        {{ form_open(delete_form, delete_action) }}
        {{ form_row(delete_form.get('userId')) }}
        {{ form_row(delete_form.get('security')) }}
        {{ form_submit(delete_form.get('delete')) }}&nbsp;{{ form_button(delete_form.get('cancel')) }}
        {{ form_close() }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
